From: Chairman <chairman@steni.example> (Steni AS)
To: CEP/Mike Barton/Dave Allen <m.barton@cep-holdings.example> (CEP Holdings Ltd)
Date: 2004-12-21
Subject: Notice of breach under clause 7.2 of the Exclusive Distributor Agreement

Notice pursuant to clause 7.2 of the EDA. CEP has 30 days to rectify the following breaches:

1. Clause 2.3: CEP has "failed to use all reasonable endeavours to promote and sell Steni Products in the Territory, to ensure a stabile [sic] and positive growth". "During the past 3 years the historical sales in UK has been as follows: Sales 2001: 59.744 m2 Sales 2002: 53.250 m2 Sales 2003: 43.042 m2 ..." "From 2001 to 2004, there is a reduction of 62% !! in the total CEP sales of steni products. Steni has also asked for budget figures for 2005, with 2 reminders, without receiving any information or response back."

2. Aberfeldy project, clause 3.4: failure to pay the sum of EUR 18,508 due on various invoices for panels supplied by Steni for the project.

3. Aberfeldy project, clause 4.6: failure to deliver a claim report detailing the customer's complaint.

4. Aberfeldy project, clause 4.7: entering into a settlement with the customer granting it a price reduction of EUR 18,508, giving the customer terms more favourable than those in Appendix III.

Steni AS

